sentences.text:
In this petition, petitioner seeks the following relief:
"(a) Quash the charge sheet filed by the Respondent No.1 Police in Crime No.291/2024 registered as C.C.No.516/2025 for the offence p/u/s 498A, 504, 506 of the Indian Penal Code and Section 3 and 4 of the Dowry Prohibition Act, 1961,
pending on the file of the 2nd Additional CJM Court, Bangalore Rural Bengaluru District, Bengaluru in respect of the petitioner herein vide Annexure-A;
Sri Kumar V vs State Of Karnataka on 8 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/82385830/
2 NC: 2025:KHC:24868 HC-KAR (b) Quash the entire proceedings in C.C.No.516/2025 pending on the file of the Court the 2nd Additional CJM Court, Bangalore Rural Bengaluru District, Bengaluru in respect of the petitioner herein vide Annexure K;
(c) Quash the order dated 22.02.2025 passed in C.C.No.516/2025 taking cognizance for offences punishable under Section 498A, 504, 506 of the Indian Penal Code and Section 3 and 4 of the Dowry Prohibition Act, 1961 pending on the file of the 2nd Additional CJM Court, Bangalore Rural Bengaluru District, Bengaluru, in respect of the petitioner herein vide Annexure-K;

